// Calibration: Block on Contradiction
// Purpose: Hard safety gate when tool results disagree
// Category: Data Quality → Safety Gate (Hard Block)
// Use Case: mcp-trace-gate scenarios, multi-source data inconsistency
// 
// WHAT IS CONTRADICTION?
// When two tools return conflicting data on the same identity field.
// Example:
//   - Tool A: user_id = "123", status = "active"
//   - Tool B: user_id = "123", status = "inactive"
//   → contradiction = true (disagreement on shared identity field)
//
// WHY THIS MATTERS (APM Blind Spot)
// Standard distributed tracing logs:
//   - Tool A: ✅ 200 OK, 45ms
//   - Tool B: ✅ 200 OK, 38ms
// Both appear healthy. But they contradict each other on critical data.
// CEL detects this; logs don't.
//
// VERDICT: BLOCK execution immediately
// This is a hard safety gate: no human override without review.

contradiction == true
